WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.347
Relations-oriented behavior: build the people.

2
00:00:04.397 --> 00:00:10.915
In Yukl’s taxonomy this is category two of four, behaviors five to eight of fifteen,

3
00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:18.344
and its objective is to build the quality of the people and the relationships the work runs on.

4
00:00:18.394 --> 00:00:23.036
It is where Vanderbilt’s engagement scores are made or lost.

5
00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:30.620
Behavior five, supporting: someone mentions a hard week at home; you listen, adjust what you can,

6
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.497
and follow up on Monday.

7
00:00:32.547 --> 00:00:41.099
Know where support ends and a duty begins: a possible leave request goes to leave administration the same day,

8
00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:49.544
and you never ask for a diagnosis. Behavior six, developing: once a quarter, without a form in front of you,

9
00:00:49.594 --> 00:00:56.816
ask what each person wants to be doing in two years and find one stretch assignment to match.

10
00:00:56.866 --> 00:01:04.401
Behavior seven, recognizing: the way you handled the vendor call on Thursday kept us on schedule,

11
00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:08.232
said on Friday. Specific, named, within the week.

12
00:01:08.282 --> 00:01:16.286
Great job everyone names nobody. Behavior eight, empowering: hand over the decision, not only the task,

13
00:01:16.336 --> 00:01:19.883
and ask the team before you set a new process.

14
00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:24.027
Watch for the difference. Friendly is not supporting.

15
00:01:24.077 --> 00:01:26.842
The annual review is not developing.

16
00:01:26.892 --> 00:01:35.444
Now flip the four cards, then turn the page for a conversation that is half personal and half a leave request.

